3127:Indeed, in 2-D the interpolation scheme is built specifically such that a uniform velocity field is exactly interpolated by Eq. (<a href="https://gmd.copernicus.org/articles/12/3571/2019/#Ch1.E10" class="scrollto" data-fixed-element=".auto-fixed-top-forced.article-title">10</a>) (see demonstration in Sect. <a href="https://gmd.copernicus.org/articles/12/3571/2019/#Ch1.S3.SS1" class="scrollto" data-fixed-element=".auto-fixed-top-forced.article-title">3.1</a>). This is made possible since when developing the right-hand side of Eq. (<a href="https://gmd.copernicus.org/articles/12/3571/2019/#Ch1.E10" class="scrollto" data-fixed-element=".auto-fixed-top-forced.article-title">10</a>), one obtains a numerator which is a bilinear function of <span class="inline-formula"><i>ξ</i></span> and <span class="inline-formula"><i>η</i></span> and a denominator which is the Jacobian, precisely bilinear in <span class="inline-formula"><i>ξ</i></span> and<span id="page3575"></span> <span class="inline-formula"><i>η</i></span>.
